{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>If torn he shall be torn, he shall bring it as witness.</b> The remnant that is found of the torn animal — he shall bring it to serve as his witness that it was torn and that it was taken from him by force. And we find this practice among shepherds, whose way is to exert themselves until they find a small part of the torn animal to bring before the owners, and they are exempt. And so it is written in Hosea: 'as the shepherd rescues from the mouth of the lion and from the mouth of the bear two legs or a piece of an ear' etc. — one may wonder, what does the shepherd have to rescue such a small thing for? But surely it is for this purpose."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:46.597868291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}